import{_ as o,o as t,c as s,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Task — Content Writing View (FR 3.6.10)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/content-task-workflow/3-6-10-content-writting-view/task.md","filePath":"feature/content-task-workflow/3-6-10-content-writting-view/task.md"}'),i={name:"feature/content-task-workflow/3-6-10-content-writting-view/task.md"};function a(r,e,d,c,l,p){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="task-—-content-writing-view-fr-3-6-10" tabindex="-1">Task — Content Writing View (FR 3.6.10) <a class="header-anchor" href="#task-—-content-writing-view-fr-3-6-10" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Task — Content Writing View (FR 3.6.10)&quot;">​</a></h1><p>&gt; Status: <strong>Implemented</strong> (V5, 2026-10-26: Docs/Word hybrid UI redesign + presence/multi-cursor awareness + React Native mobile port — see items 13–15 below; V4: canvas + Yjs CRDT real-time sync — see <a href="./spec.html">spec.md</a>, <a href="./plan.html">plan.md</a>). Remaining items below are explicitly out of scope for this pass, not blockers.</p><ul><li><p>[x] <strong>0. Prerequisite</strong>: minimal <code>Task</code> entity + basic CRUD — <strong>implemented</strong>, but intentionally not the full FR 3.6.1 Identify Task Detail scope (no assignee, due date, comments). See <code>Task.java</code>, <code>TaskService(Impl).java</code>, <code>TaskController.java</code>.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>1. Data model</strong>: <code>TaskContentOperation</code> (append-only, opaque base64 Yjs update log), <code>TaskContentSnapshot</code> (client-reported Yjs state), migrations applied to local DB.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>2. OT architecture decision</strong>: direction B chosen and implemented — Yjs CRDT, not hand-written OT. See <a href="./plan.html#6-technical-risks-as-realized">plan.md §6</a>.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>3. WebSocket infra (BE)</strong>: <code>spring-boot-starter-websocket</code> added, <code>WebSocketConfig</code> (STOMP endpoint <code>/ws/tasks</code>, broker <code>/topic</code>), <code>WsJwtHandshakeInterceptor</code> (JWT via query param, reuses <code>JwtUtil</code>), <code>SecurityConfig</code>/<code>JwtAuthenticationFilter</code> updated to permit the WS path at the HTTP layer.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>4. Canvas rendering engine (FE)</strong> — implemented and browser-verified at <code>/content-writing</code>: text layout/measurement, line-breaking, render loop. See <code>brandhub-web-dashboard/src/pages/content-writing/</code>.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>5. Offscreen input capture (FE)</strong> — implemented and browser-verified: hidden off-screen <code>contenteditable</code>, Vietnamese IME handling (verified with a synthesized composition sequence), CSS cursor overlay, canvas click-to-position, Backspace/Delete. Text selection (highlighting a range) not implemented. Route gated to CREATOR/MANAGER via <code>ROUTE_ACCESS[&quot;/content-writing&quot;]</code> (FE) and <code>@RequireRole</code> (BE).</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>6. Real-time sync (FE+BE)</strong>: <code>useTaskContentSync</code> hook — STOMP client (<code>@stomp/stompjs</code>), Yjs <code>Y.Doc</code> wired to <code>CanvasTextEditor</code>, <code>TaskContentWebSocketController</code> persists + broadcasts updates. Browser-verified single-client: type → persisted via WS → reload → content restored correctly from snapshot+operations, in the right order. <strong>Not yet verified with two concurrent browser sessions</strong> (multi-client convergence is implemented per the Yjs/STOMP design but not manually tested end-to-end).</p><ul><li><strong>Bug found and fixed during verification</strong>: <code>appendOperation</code>&#39;s <code>count(taskId) + 1</code> sequence assignment was not atomic — concurrent WS messages for the same Task could compute the same <code>sequenceNumber</code>, the loser&#39;s INSERT hit the unique constraint and threw, and that update was silently lost (never persisted, never broadcast). A later Yjs struct whose <code>origin</code> pointed at the lost one became a permanently unreachable orphan, which looked like &quot;most of what I typed disappeared after reload.&quot; Fixed with a per-task <code>synchronized</code> lock in <code>TaskContentServiceImpl.appendOperation</code>. Also fixed two related client-side bugs found along the way: a stale <code>caretIndex</code> closure in <code>CanvasTextEditor</code>&#39;s insert/delete handlers (now backed by a ref), and a missing <code>yDoc.off()</code> cleanup for the local-update listener in <code>useTaskContentSync</code>.</li><li>Typing fast enough (e.g. scripted <code>type_text</code>-style bulk input near-simultaneously) can still drop a keystroke client-side before it reaches the Y.Doc update event — not reproduced with normal human-speed typing in this verification; flagged here rather than silently ignored.</li></ul></li><li><p>[x] <strong>12. Automated tests (2026-10-12)</strong>: 47 Vitest + 22 JUnit + 18 Playwright + 31 live-backend integration, all passing — see <a href="./test.html">test.md</a>. The live run found three backend defects the mocks hid: (a) the chat feature&#39;s global STOMP interceptor blocked <code>/ws/tasks</code> entirely (CONNECT needed an <code>Authorization</code> header, only chat destinations allowed) — real-time sync was dead; (b) no workspace-membership check on task content SEND/SUBSCRIBE (fixed in parallel upstream via <code>authorizeTask</code>); (c) the per-task lock from item 6 sat inside <code>@Transactional</code>, so it released before commit and a 120-update burst lost ~half the updates (<code>@Transactional</code> removed from <code>appendOperation</code>). All fixed and re-verified. The &quot;Bug found and fixed&quot; note under item 6 was therefore only partly true until this fix. Testing also found and fixed: toolbar click dropped editor focus (list items couldn&#39;t be typed straight after), and an IME render loop (<code>Maximum update depth exceeded</code>) in <code>CanvasTextEditor</code> (<code>displayRuns</code> not memoized). Not covered: real-backend integration, two live tabs, HTTP-level test of the new version endpoint (test.md §6).</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>7. Accessibility</strong> (partial, 2026-10-12): the <code>aria-live</code> text mirror (verified in sync) plus the hidden input is now <code>role=textbox</code> <code>aria-multiline</code> and the canvas is <code>aria-hidden</code> (E2E-20). Not done: a real screen-reader pass (NVDA/VoiceOver); <code>aria-live=&quot;polite&quot;</code> re-announcing the whole text on each change may be noisy and needs tuning with real assistive tech.</p></li><li><p>[ ] <strong>8. Virtualization</strong>: not implemented — content is short-form (social posts), so a single canvas without pagination was judged sufficient for this scope.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>9. Version History</strong>: REST load/list/restore snapshot implemented (<code>TaskContentServiceImpl</code>), <code>VersionHistorySidebar</code> UI implemented. Browser-verified: reporting a snapshot via REST makes it appear in the sidebar, and clicking Restore completes without error.</p><ul><li><strong>Fixed (2026-10-12)</strong>: (a) <em>Restore</em> previously only remounted the editor and appended a snapshot whose <code>sequenceNumber</code> collided with the next operation (that edit was dropped on reload). Now <code>restoreVersion</code> is read-only and the client applies the old content to the live <code>Y.Doc</code> as a normal edit (delete + <code>applyDelta</code>), so it persists, broadcasts to other clients, and keeps the log append-only. (b) The versions API now returns <code>editedBy</code> / <code>editedByName</code> (last editor included in the snapshot) and the sidebar shows it (&quot;who&quot;).</li><li><strong>Added (2026-10-12)</strong>: (c) per-version <em>diff</em> — new <code>GET .../content/versions/{snapshotId}</code> returns that version&#39;s Yjs state; the sidebar decodes it and shows a word-level diff against the previous version (<code>contentUtils.diffText</code>). (d) Snapshots are also reported after 20 s idle and on leaving the page (not only every 200 operations), so short posts get versions; the sidebar refreshes after each report.</li></ul></li><li><p><strong>Lists (AC &quot;bold, italic, list, emoji&quot;)</strong>: bullet / numbered buttons in <code>FormattingToolbar</code>; implemented as literal text prefixes (<code>• </code>, <code>1. </code>) so the published text matches what&#39;s shown. Enter inside an item continues the list; Enter on an empty item exits it. Known limits: no hanging indent on wrapped lines, inserting mid-list doesn&#39;t renumber following items.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>10. Offline queue</strong> (2026-10-12): edits made while disconnected are queued in memory and persisted in <code>localStorage</code>, flushed on reconnect; on reconnect the log is re-read so missed remote updates merge in; reconnect uses a fresh token (E2E-19). Chose localStorage over IndexedDB since queued Yjs updates are small; revisit if long offline sessions are expected.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>11. Font auto-conversion on publish</strong>: <code>toPublishText()</code> in <code>contentUtils.ts</code> NFC-normalizes Vietnamese text and converts bold/italic runs to Unicode styled letters (Mathematical Sans-Serif; Vietnamese base letters styled with combining marks kept, <code>đ/Đ</code> stay plain). The Social Preview shows this converted text and a &quot;Sao chép bản đăng&quot; button copies it. <strong>Not yet wired to an actual publish action</strong> — no publish flow exists for Content Writing Tasks yet; the E52 publisher should call <code>toPublishText()</code> on the same delta. Styled-letter rendering of Vietnamese diacritics varies by platform/font — verify on target platforms.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>13. Docs/Word hybrid UI redesign (2026-10-26)</strong>: <code>CanvasTextEditor.tsx</code> now renders the canvas on a white &quot;paper&quot; sheet (<code>max-w-[816px]</code>, Docs/Word page proportions) over a gray desk background; <code>FormattingToolbar.tsx</code> gained a Docs/Ribbon mode toggle (<code>ToolGroup</code> wrapper — flat row in Docs mode, captioned groups in Ribbon mode). Purely visual: same props, same handlers, same Yjs wiring — verified by running the existing 20 E2E tests unmodified both before and after, all green both times. REA skill (binary reverse-engineering) was tried against a local <code>WINWORD.EXE</code> install first per explicit user request, found no usable UI assets (modern Office ships ribbon chrome as runtime theme/XML, not classic <code>RT_ICON</code> resources — confirmed via <code>inspect_pe_resources</code>: only 13 legacy icon groups, rest opaque metadata), so the redesign used direct knowledge of Docs/Word UI conventions instead. <code>ponytail:ponytail-review</code> run against the diff: &quot;Lean already. Ship.&quot;</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>14. Presence / multi-cursor awareness (2026-10-26)</strong>: new backend endpoint <code>TaskContentWebSocketController.handleAwareness</code> (<code>/app+/topic/tasks/{taskId}/awareness</code>, unpersisted relay, same opaque-blob posture as content). Frontend: <code>useTaskContentSync.ts</code> creates a <code>y-protocols/awareness</code> <code>Awareness</code> instance per <code>Y.Doc</code>, publishes local cursor/selection on change, subscribes to peers, exposes <code>peers</code>/<code>updateLocalCursor</code>; <code>CanvasTextEditor.tsx</code> renders peer cursor flags (colored line + name label) computed via the same <code>caretCoordsFromIndex</code> math as the local caret; <code>index.tsx</code> shows peer avatar initials in the status bar. Colors are deterministic per user ID (<code>colorForUser</code>, FNV-ish hash into a 10-color palette) so a peer&#39;s color stays stable across sessions. 2 new E2E tests (E2E-21, E2E-22) plus a test-infrastructure fix (<code>tests/e2e/editor/content-writing.spec.ts</code>&#39;s mock STOMP broker now tracks awareness sends separately from content sends — they were being conflated into one counter, which silently broke 3 pre-existing tests the moment awareness started publishing; fixed by giving the broker an <code>awarenessSent</code> array and a <code>simulatePeerAwareness</code> helper that targets the real subscription id a fake peer&#39;s <code>MESSAGE</code> must match).</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>15. React Native mobile port (2026-10-26)</strong>: <code>brandhub-mobile-app/src/screens/content-writing/</code> — same Yjs CRDT sync protocol as web (<code>useTaskContentSync.ts</code>, same REST + STOMP contract, ported <code>richText.ts</code>/<code>listUtils.ts</code>/<code>contentUtils.ts</code> logic verbatim or near-verbatim), rendered through a native <code>TextInput</code> (<code>RichTextEditor.tsx</code>) instead of canvas (RN has no <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> without <code>react-native-skia</code>, confirmed out of scope by explicit user choice — see spec.md&#39;s Out of Scope). Covers: realtime sync, bold/italic/underline/strikethrough/align/lists/undo/redo (<code>FormattingToolbar.tsx</code>), version history + restore + diff (<code>VersionHistory.tsx</code>), 3-platform social preview (<code>SocialPreview.tsx</code>), presence (avatar initials only, no live cursor marker — RN TextInput has no per-character pixel coordinate API). New screen <code>ContentWritingEditorScreen.tsx</code> wired into <code>MoreStackNavigator.tsx</code> as route <code>ContentWritingEditor</code>; <code>ContentWritingScreen.tsx</code> (task list) now navigates there instead of to <code>TaskDetail</code>, plus a &quot;Bài viết mới&quot; button. New dependencies: <code>yjs</code>, <code>y-protocols</code>, <code>@stomp/stompjs</code>, <code>react-native-get-random-values</code> (real-device crypto polyfill, also fixes Jest — see test.md §8). 22 new Jest unit tests (<code>listUtils</code>/<code>base64</code>/<code>contentUtils</code>), full existing 53-test mobile suite has zero regressions, project-wide <code>tsc --noEmit</code> clean.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>16. Mobile feature-parity closeout (2026-10-26, same day)</strong>: closed the three gaps item 15 had flagged as out of scope, after explicit user request to finish them. <code>richText.ts</code>&#39;s <code>RunAttrs</code> gained <code>highlight</code>/<code>font</code>/<code>size</code>/<code>link</code> (matching web); <code>FormattingToolbar.tsx</code> gained a Docs/Ribbon mode switch (flat row vs. captioned groups — a lighter visual variant of web&#39;s toggle, not a literal port of Word&#39;s full ribbon chrome, since a phone width has no room for that), color/highlight swatch pickers (<code>Modal</code> + grid of <code>Pressable</code> swatches), font/size <code>Select</code> dropdowns, and a link <code>Modal</code> with a URL <code>Input</code>; <code>ContentWritingEditorScreen.tsx</code> gained image attachment (<code>expo-image-picker</code>, already a project dependency — reused the exact permission/launch pattern from <code>TaskUploadScreen.tsx</code>), capped at 6 images with a thumbnail strip + remove button, wired into <code>SocialPreview</code>. 5 new icons added to <code>Icons.tsx</code> (<code>Link2Icon</code>, <code>PaletteIcon</code>, <code>HighlighterIcon</code>, <code>RowsIcon</code>; <code>GridIcon</code> already existed).</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>17. Mobile component tests + Maestro device flows (2026-10-26, same day)</strong>: the two gaps item 16 had left explicitly deferred, closed on further explicit request. 24 new <code>@testing-library/react-native</code> component tests across 4 files (<code>FormattingToolbar.test.tsx</code> 9, <code>SocialPreview.test.tsx</code> 6, <code>VersionHistory.test.tsx</code> 3, <code>RichTextEditor.test.tsx</code> 6 — the last against a real <code>Y.Doc</code>, not a mock, so it also exercises the Yjs CRDT wiring). <strong>Found and fixed a real test-isolation bug while writing these</strong>: <code>fireEvent.press</code> in this RTL (14.1.0) + React 19 combo must be wrapped in <code>await act(async () =&gt; ...)</code> — without it, the state update from one test&#39;s press leaks past that test&#39;s boundary and corrupts the <em>next</em> test&#39;s <code>render()</code> in the same file (it silently fails to mount — <code>toJSON()</code> returns <code>null</code> — surfacing only as a confusing &quot;unable to find element&quot; on an unrelated query, with no stack trace pointing at the real cause). Root-caused via a binary-search probe (isolated <code>Modal</code>-only and <code>Select</code>-only renders first, both fine; then reproduced the exact failing 3-test sequence outside the real file to confirm the <code>act()</code> fix). Also added Maestro device-flow YAML (<code>.maestro/content-writing/*.yaml</code>, 5 flows) and a setup README — <strong>written but not executed</strong>: no Maestro install and no running simulator/emulator were available in this session; see <code>.maestro/README.md</code> for install steps and what each flow covers/doesn&#39;t.</p></li><li><p>[x] <strong>18. Maestro closeout — version history + offline/reconnect flows (2026-10-26, same day)</strong>: the two single-device gaps item 17&#39;s README had listed as &quot;not covered&quot; are now covered: <code>06-version-history.yaml</code> (type → autosave snapshot → diff toggle → restore) and <code>07-offline-reconnect.yaml</code> (airplane-mode edit → local queue → reconnect → flush, <strong>Android-only</strong>, <code>setAirplaneMode</code> has no iOS equivalent). Same caveat as item 17: written, not executed, no Maestro/emulator available this session. Still genuinely not coverable by any single-device flow: two-device real-time sync and presence/multi-cursor (both need two simultaneous driven sessions against the same task — real for both web E2E and Maestro, not a tooling gap specific to one).</p></li></ul>',3)])])}const m=o(i,[["render",a]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
